# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore — SEC-009 SCA gate allowlist (grading.hrlab.uz)
# =============================================================================
# This is the EXPLICIT, per-CVE allowlist for the CI dependency/SCA gate in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml (jobs "03 · backend-deps-scan" and
# "04 · frontend-deps-scan"). trivy reads it via `--ignorefile .trivyignore`.
# Any id listed here is suppressed for the `trivy fs` scan and will NOT block
# the build. It does NOT affect deploy.yml (production deploy is decoupled from
# the ci quality matrix by design — do not re-wire it here).
#
# POLICY (read before adding anything):
#   * The gate blocks only FIXABLE (patch-available) HIGH/CRITICAL findings
#     (`--ignore-unfixed`). The correct first response to a finding is to BUMP
#     the dependency, NOT to allowlist it.
#   * Allowlist a CVE ONLY when a fix is not yet available, the upgrade is
#     genuinely blocked, or the vuln is not exploitable in this app — and only
#     with security sign-off.
#   * Every entry MUST be a single CVE/GHSA id — NO blanket or wildcard ignores —
#     and MUST carry, in the comment block directly above it:
#       - Justification (why it is accepted / not exploitable here)
#       - Owner / approver
#       - Review-by date (re-evaluate on/before this date; default +90 days)
#   * Entries past their Review-by date must be re-justified or removed. Treat
#     this file as auditable, time-boxed security debt — not a mute button.
#
# FORMAT (one id per line):
#
#   # Justification: <why accepted / not exploitable in this app>
#   # Owner: <name/role>   Review-by: <YYYY-MM-DD>
#   CVE-XXXX-XXXXX
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO ACTIVE SUPPRESSIONS.
#
# The FIRST gated CI run is expected to surface pre-existing FIXABLE
# HIGH/CRITICAL findings (see the SEC-009 report). The most likely tripwire is
# the embedded Tomcat shipped transitively by Spring Boot 3.3.4 (end-of-OSS-
# support), e.g. CVE-2025-24813 (CVSS 9.8). Each surfaced finding must be either
# FIXED (bump the dependency — preferred) or added below WITH a justification
# and a review date. Do NOT blanket-ignore.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Example (commented out — copy the shape, never leave a bare id):
# # Justification: no fix released upstream yet; the affected code path (feature
# #   X) is disabled in SecurityConfig, so it is not reachable in this deployment.
# # Owner: security-engineer   Review-by: 2026-10-08
# CVE-2025-00000
